  <h2>Future Vision: From Retreat to Longevity Research</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Note: Everything below is aspirational.</strong> These phases depend on the retreat center
    being built and operational first, plus securing medical partnerships, funding, and regulatory approval.
    No longevity facilities, staff, or protocols exist yet.
  </p>
  <p>
    The retreat center's biometric monitoring infrastructure could, over time, serve as a foundation
    for health research. The potential evolution:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Phase 1: Quantified wellness (where we start)</strong> — Biometric monitoring, EEG, HRV during retreat programs. Real physiological data collection that builds the community's capacity for health technology.</li>
    <li><strong>Phase 2: Health baselines (planned)</strong> — On-site blood panels, metabolic testing, sleep analysis. Guests leave with a health baseline they can track over time. Requires the Techno Park to build or source instruments.</li>
    <li><strong>Phase 3: Longevity research (aspirational)</strong> — Partnerships with longevity researchers. Extended programs exploring aging interventions: NAD+ protocols, senolytics, epigenetic testing. Subject to regulatory approval and qualified medical staff.</li>
    <li><strong>Phase 4: Longevity district (long-term vision)</strong> — Housing for long-term residents focused on healthy lifespan extension. Integrated with research facilities, organic food production, and community support. Years away and contingent on all prior phases succeeding.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For the full longevity research vision, see the <a href="/en/health#longevity" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">Health & Wellness page</a>.
  </p>

